{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["דן ידין עמו — the commentator who explains this as referring to Shimshon did not know the depth of the plain sense of Scripture at all. Did Yaakov come to prophesy about a man who fell into the hands of the Pelishtim and they gouged out his eyes and he died with the Pelishtim in an evil matter?! Far be it, far be it. Rather, he prophesied about the tribe of Dan that it is the rear-guard (מאסף) for all the camps. And so in Yehoshua it is written: ״והמאסף הולך אחר הארון״. And since it went all the days, both in the days of Moshe and in the days of Yehoshua, behind all the banners, and it had to fight against all the nations that pursued them to attack the rear, to cut down all the stragglers behind them on the way, and to take vengeance on the nations — for they were mighty — therefore Yaakov said: דן ידין עמו — he will avenge the vengeance of his people." "כאחד — all." "שבטי ישראל — he would avenge their vengeance and guard them from their pursuers, as in: ״כי ידין ה׳ את עמו״ וגו׳, and: ״ודם עבדיו יקום ונקם ישיב לצריו״, and similarly: ״ידין בגוים מלא גויות מחץ ראש על ארץ רבה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The lemma והמאסף הולך אחר הארון corresponds to Joshua 6:13 (referring to the rear-guard); the phrase 'בענין רע' is rendered hyper-literally as 'in an evil matter'."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:48.894570708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}